### Most worth attention

Chosen by rule: errors in own layers, by rule, most findings first; then layer structure errors (org/layer-conf errors outside own layers, bbappends outside own layers that match no recipe: BitBake stops on these); then warnings in own layers, by rule; while that gives fewer than 3: errors in upstream layers by rule, then layer structure warnings, then infos in own layers by rule; at most 10.

1. **warning** `hygiene/release-syntax` (1 finding, in meta-mine): `meta-mine:recipes-app/app/app_0.1.bb:22` `${WORKDIR}/app.c`: from styhead on, `file://` sources are unpacked into ${UNPACKDIR}, not ${WORKDIR}, and this layer is checked against wrynose; write `${UNPACKDIR}/app.c` (or `${S}/app.c` with S = "${UNPACKDIR}")
2. **warning** `org/append-no-match` (1 finding, in meta-mine): `meta-mine:recipes-app/orphan/orphan_9.%.bbappend:1` orphan_9.%.bbappend matches no recipe in the workspace, which BitBake treats as an error ("No recipes available for"); there is no orphan recipe; remove the append or add its layer
3. **warning** `override/plus-equals-on-default` (1 finding, in build): `build:conf/local.conf:13` `DISTRO_FEATURES +=` gives DISTRO_FEATURES a value before the `?=` default at meta-core:conf/distro/testdistro.conf:5 is parsed, so that default is lost; write `DISTRO_FEATURES:append = " wayland"`

