## 4. Lint findings

7 findings in 21 files: own layers and build directory 4 (0 error, 3 warning, 1 info); upstream layers 3 (0 error, 1 warning, 2 info)

Every enabled rule over every layer, as `sous-chef lint --all`: upstream layers are checked against the workspace release alone, own layers against every release they claim. Commands below assume the global flags this audit was run with (`--config`, `--build-dir`), run from the root.

### Own layers and the build directory

#### build (2 findings: 0 error, 1 warning, 1 info)

- `override/plus-equals-on-default` (warning, 1)
  - `build:conf/local.conf:13`: `DISTRO_FEATURES +=` gives DISTRO_FEATURES a value before the `?=` default at meta-core:conf/distro/testdistro.conf:5 is parsed, so that default is lost; write `DISTRO_FEATURES:append = " wayland"`

- `org/recipe-change-in-local-conf` (info, 1)
  - `build:conf/local.conf:9`: `EXTRA_OECONF:append:pn-hello` in local.conf changes only recipe hello, and only in this build directory; move it to a hello_%.bbappend in your layer as `EXTRA_OECONF:append`, or to your distro conf if it is policy

#### meta-mine (2 findings: 0 error, 2 warning, 0 info)

- `hygiene/release-syntax` (warning, 1)
  - `meta-mine:recipes-app/app/app_0.1.bb:22`: `${WORKDIR}/app.c`: from styhead on, `file://` sources are unpacked into ${UNPACKDIR}, not ${WORKDIR}, and this layer is checked against wrynose; write `${UNPACKDIR}/app.c` (or `${S}/app.c` with S = "${UNPACKDIR}")

- `org/append-no-match` (warning, 1)
  - `meta-mine:recipes-app/orphan/orphan_9.%.bbappend:1`: orphan_9.%.bbappend matches no recipe in the workspace, which BitBake treats as an error ("No recipes available for"); there is no orphan recipe; remove the append or add its layer

